{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>From those who slaughter the slaughter.</b> Meaning: those who perform ordinary slaughter, and it does not speak of slaughtering an actual sacrifice — for the foreleg, cheeks, and stomach apply to profane meat but not to consecrated meat, as it concludes in tractate חולין, chapter הזרוע." "<b>Those who slaughter</b> — to include the animal of partners."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:03.675139003Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}